los angeles has a high crime rate  but the violent nature of this attack  has shocked many here in west hollywood  paramedics treating a dog walker after  he was shot four times in the chest  with a semi-automatic weapon two dogs  were stolen  it very quickly emerged the owner of the  pets was singer lady gaga  a neighbor who witnessed the attack told  sky news  it felt targeted i looked over the fence  hearing the screaming because i might  have to go outside and see what's going  on and that's when the gunshot went off  right like that so i'm not going out now  so i turned around and ran back in the  house with my dog and my  partner and then i heard a second  gunshot and that's when i called 9-1-1  and there was a white car with two doors  open and  i saw a little scuffle there but that's  when i that gunshot happened it happened  literally 30 seconds i came back out and  i saw the guy on the ground  and everybody was on top of him just  like holding him even though it was  lady gaga's dogs i don't care a guy got  shot and he was  laying there on the ground like i  thought he was dead  lady gaga has now reportedly offered  half a million dollars for the safe  return of her two french bulldogs  no questions asked setting up an email  address in the dog's names  as a means of contact there are  shootings every day in los angeles  but the intense media interest in this  crime  is of course because of the celebrity  involved and now  the big money involved in terms of this  reported reward  could make other high-profile people  more vulnerable to this sort of crime  it's unclear if the attack was intended  to elicit a ransom  but there's concern it could inspire  others to carry out similar crimes  it sets a precedent that could backfire  um there could be copycat  robberies that take place with people  looking to get such huge windfalls from  celebrities  um and in general it kind of sends the  message  that some celebrities may be willing to  pay out a lot of money  without with few consequences in order  to get those types of belongings and  prize  possessions and animals back thankfully  the dog walker is said to be recovering  well  and police are continuing to search for  those behind the attack  sally lockwood sky news los angeles
 

